ther for aggravated kidnapping. NEWLINE_CHAR NEWLINE_CHAR Prison officials said sources for years had told them Salaz was hiding out in Mexico but he managed to evade police. The hunt for him involved the U.S. Marshals Service, the Texas prison system's Office of Inspector General and Mexican law enforcement agencies. NEWLINE_CHAR NEWLINE_CHAR \"Salaz thought that he had eluded authorities by starting a new life in Mexico,\" Department of Criminal Justice Inspector General Bruce Toney said Wednesday. \"He was wrong.\" NEWLINE_CHAR NEWLINE_CHAR Salaz is to be returned to Texas custody once the Mexican government approves his extradition. NEWLINE_CHAR NEWLINE_CHAR Salaz's capture leaves Jose Fernando Bustos-Diaz, 24, as the lone Texas prison fugitive. He fled in April 2010 from the Brisco Unit in Dilley, near San Antonio. The prison houses medium- and minimum-security inmates. He also is believed to have fled to Mexico. NEWLINE_CHAR NEWLINE_CHAR Bustos-Diaz was serving 35 years for a 2005 murder in Harris County. ||||| Page 1 of 1 NEWLINE_CHAR NEWLINE_CHAR Former Houston Police Department homicide detective Jim Binford shows the bullet that was \ufeffremoved from his body after \ufeffa shootout \ufeffinvolving fugitive Jose Salaz in April \ufeff1995. NEWLINE_CHAR NEWLINE_CHAR Jose Salaz is the only prisoner to escape from the Texas prison system and still remain at large. NEWLINE_CHAR NEWLINE_CHAR A man who escaped from a Texas prison 16 years ago has been captured in Mexico, authorities said Wednesday. NEWLINE_CHAR NEWLINE_CHAR Juan Salaz, an American citizen, was captured last week and remains in Mexico awaiting extradition, authorities said. NEWLINE_CHAR NEWLINE_CHAR Salaz escaped on March 22, 1997 from the Garza East Unit in Beeville, southeast of San Antonio. He was serving three concurrent 35 years sentences for two counts of attempted capital murder of a police officer and aggravated kidnapping with a deadly weapon. NEWLINE_CHAR NEWLINE_CHAR He climbed over three 16-foot razor wire topped security fences. NEWLINE_CHAR NEWLINE_CHAR As recently as three years ago, investigators suspected Salaz was is in the vicinity of Monterrey, Mexico. At that time, investigators said they suspected Salaz has crossed back and forth between Mexico and Texas with help from family in Houston.\n",
